# Copy to .env for local dev, or set as a secret on the actual deployment
# target — `.env*` is gitignored so nothing here ever gets committed.

# HTTP RPC used by app/api/pay/solana/route.ts to fetch a recent blockhash
# when building the split (creator + 0.08% Propz fee) transaction. The
# server only ever reads chain state through this — it never signs or
# holds funds. Falls back to the public mainnet-beta endpoint if unset,
# which works for local testing only — Cloudflare Workers' shared egress
# IPs get outright blocked by it in production ("Your IP or provider is
# blocked from this endpoint"), confirmed by hitting it from a deployed
# Worker.
#
# Production (propz.saylorinnovations.com) is currently set to
# https://solana-rpc.publicnode.com — free, no signup, no key, and load-
# tested clean (20 concurrent requests, no rate-limiting) before being
# wired in. Good enough for early usage; if traffic grows enough that it
# stops being enough, move to a paid provider (Helius, Triton, etc.) —
# nothing else in the app needs to change, just this one secret:
#   wrangler secret put SOLANA_RPC_URL
SOLANA_RPC_URL=
